From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: report in-flight TX frames when the datapath is freed

ath11k_dp_free() releases the frames still queued on the host TX rings with
dev_kfree_skb_any(). mac80211 never hears about them, so a frame whose sender
waits for its TX status (control-port or nl80211 TX with a wait,
SO_WIFI_STATUS) keeps its entry in local->ack_status_frames, and the driver
unload after a firmware crash ends in

  Have pending ack frames!
  WARNING: ... at net/mac80211/main.c:1716 ieee80211_free_ack_frame
    ieee80211_free_hw <- ath11k_mac_destroy <- ath11k_core_deinit
    <- ath11k_ahb_remove

Report them with ieee80211_free_txskb() instead, as the TX completion path
already does for the frames it drops. ath11k_dp_free() runs before
ath11k_mac_destroy(), so the hw is still allocated, and on the crash-recovery
path it is still registered.

Measured on an RD03v2 (IPQ5018 + QCN6122, host-mode Wi-Fi): a Q6 assert
followed by the watchdog's driver reload produced the warning on every run; a
healthy wifi down plus rmmod/modprobe produced none.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.c
@@ -1067,11 +1067,21 @@ void ath11k_dp_vdev_tx_attach(struct ath11k *ar, struct ath11k_vif *arvif)
 static int ath11k_dp_tx_pending_cleanup(struct ath11k_base *ab, void *skb)
 {
 	struct sk_buff *msdu = skb;
+	struct ath11k_skb_cb *skb_cb = ATH11K_SKB_CB(msdu);
 
-	dma_unmap_single(ab->dev, ATH11K_SKB_CB(msdu)->paddr, msdu->len,
-			 DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+	dma_unmap_single(ab->dev, skb_cb->paddr, msdu->len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 
-	dev_kfree_skb_any(msdu);
+	/*
+	 * These frames were still in flight when the firmware went away. Hand
+	 * them back to mac80211 as dropped instead of freeing them here: a
+	 * frame whose sender waits for its TX status stays in mac80211's
+	 * ack_status_frames until it is reported, and ieee80211_free_hw()
+	 * warns about every one left ("Have pending ack frames!").
+	 */
+	if (skb_cb->ar)
+		ieee80211_free_txskb(skb_cb->ar->hw, msdu);
+	else
+		dev_kfree_skb_any(msdu);
 
 	return 0;
 }
